The filler text in corpus/corpus.jsonl.gz

The haystack filler is cut from public-domain books in English. Each book is listed in corpus/books.tsv with its
title, author, Project Gutenberg ebook number, the exact text-file URL it was downloaded from and the sha256 of that
file. These works are in the public domain in the United States. If you are outside the United States, check the
copyright laws of your country before you use or share them.

The files come from Project Gutenberg (https://www.gutenberg.org). Only the text between each file's "*** START OF"
and "*** END OF" lines is used, so the Project Gutenberg licence and trademark text outside those lines is removed.
Project Gutenberg allows this for public-domain works. What remains is not a Project Gutenberg edition and is not
offered under the Project Gutenberg name or trademark.

Changes made to the texts: line endings normalised, trailing spaces removed, typographic characters mapped to ASCII
(the table is in fetch_corpus.py), and the text cut into blocks of 24 to 72 lines. Blocks were then selected and
framed as tool results or notes (corpus/blocks.tsv lists the book and line range of each block). fetch_corpus.py
rebuilds the corpus from the pinned files.

